Description: Stop-motion animation studio for kids (NEO One / ThingBot)
 NeoStopMotion is an open-source stop-motion animation studio designed
 for children aged 6-14, built for the NEO One education device
 (ARM64/Armbian) and standard Linux desktops.
 .
 Kids capture animation frames one by one using the ThingBot controller
 (two arcade buttons over UART) or the keyboard, then the app assembles
 an MP4 + GIF via ffmpeg, uploads to the cloud, and shows a QR code so
 parents can download the film.
